            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Generally a little, particularly at the budget end and at running pace. The hinge adds a joint to the frame and folding designs favour lighter construction. Well-built folding treadmills with heavier frames feel close to non-folding machines; weight is a reasonable proxy for stability.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much space does a folded treadmill save?",
